# Dashboard Web — split backend API URLs
# Copy to Dashboard Web/.env.local (never commit .env.local).
#
# The browser talks to TWO backends directly:
#   Auth-Backend      (:5712 dev) — 6 AuthN routes only
#   Dashboard-Backend (:5713 dev) — identity, app data, invites, activity, …
#
# Notify-Backend (:5715 dev) is INTERNAL ONLY — never called from the browser.
# Dashboard-Backend reaches it with INTERNAL_SERVICE_SECRET (email, SMS, push).
#
# Routing is automatic: apiPath() / apiFetch() pick Auth vs Dashboard from the path.
# See infrastructure/api/api-backend-routes.ts (must match Auth-Backend authn-paths.js).

# ── Local dev (defaults — no .env required) ───────────────────────────────────
#
# Leave all vars unset. The app uses:
#   Auth-Backend      → http://127.0.0.1:5712
#   Dashboard-Backend → http://127.0.0.1:5713
#
# Start all three backends for full functionality (email/push need Notify on :5715):
#   Auth-Backend      npm run dev   (port 5712)
#   Dashboard-Backend npm run dev   (port 5713)
#   Notify-Backend    npm run dev   (port 5715 — Dashboard calls this, not the browser)
#
# Optional overrides:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5712
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DASHBOARD_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5713

# ── Production — single API gateway (Caddy / reverse proxy) ───────────────────
#
# Set at BUILD time (NEXT_PUBLIC_* is baked into the client bundle).
# The gateway forwards the six Auth paths to vt-auth-api; everything else to vt-dashboard-api.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.myvirtualtracker.com

# ── Production — split public API hosts (no gateway) ──────────────────────────
#
# Use when Auth and Dashboard have separate subdomains. Do NOT set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_API_URL=https://auth.myvirtualtracker.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DASHBOARD_API_URL=https://dashapi.myvirtualtracker.com

# ── Do NOT add ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NOTIFY_API_URL — Notify-Backend is internal-only (Dashboard → Notify).
# SMTP, FCM, and phone validation credentials never belong in the browser bundle.
